<title>USA: Ralston Purina up on Duracell deal - analysts.</title>
<headline>Ralston Purina up on Duracell deal - analysts.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Ralston Purina Co, which makes Energizer batteries, rose 2-1/2 to 66-1/2 on news that Duracell International Inc is expected to be purchased by Gillette Co in a $7.0 billion stock merger deal.</p>
<p>Earlier, sources said the Gillette-Duracell deal is expected to be announced Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;This highlights the value of the very large...battery business,&quot; Goldman Sachs analyst Nomi Ghez said of the rise in Ralston's stock.</p>
<p>Ralston, which also makes pet foods, recently changed the name of its Eveready Battery Co to Evergizer.</p>
<p>Donaldson, Lufkin and Jenrette analyst William Leach said the battery unit, a fast-growing business, has a higher valuation than pet foods.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
